  era: "Section 36 \xB7 Indian Economy Through History \xB7 Across the ages"
  title: Indian coinage
  text: India's first coins were punch-marked silver coins, from about the 6th century BCE. Indo-Greek and Kushana coins introduced royal portraits, the Guptas issued gold dinaras, and Sher Shah Suri introduced the rupiya, ancestor of today's rupee.
